    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.comment\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI have setup mini.comment using the direction in the readme file, including the multi-language setup using tsx comments.\r\n\r\nThe problem I currently have is when using the keymap to comment in a .prisma file. As shown in the gif attached.\r\n![comment](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/95101485/207294532-c9b7aeba-1423-436c-92bb-c53c2fee4645.gif)\r\n\r\n\t\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.9.0-dev-5e1687e-dirty\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n \t1. Install mini.comment repo and setup anyway you choose\r\n    2. Open an empty file schema.prisma\r\n    3. Add a line \r\n    4. Call gcc on that line\r\n    5. You fill find that the added comment is /**/, when it should be //\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n```prisma\r\n// userId Int\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n```prisma\r\n/* userId Int */\r\n```",
